Brr includes a source fork of OpenAI Codex. The fork is pinned to the upstream
revision and records its maintained changes in runtime/UPSTREAM.md. The Codex
source retains its upstream LICENSE and NOTICE files, including notices for
third-party components. Those notices apply to the relevant portions of the
runtime.

Brr is an independent project. Mention of OpenAI Codex identifies upstream
source and does not imply sponsorship, endorsement, or affiliation.

Brr also compiles a source fork of WorkTrunk into its desktop host.
WorkTrunk is Copyright (c) 2025 Maximilian Roos and is dual-licensed under
MIT or Apache-2.0. Its upstream license is retained at vendor/worktrunk/LICENSE;
the pinned source and Brr's maintained changes are recorded in vendor/WORKTRUNK.md.

Brr's MCP form validation includes @cfworker/json-schema (MIT).
Its upstream license and third-party notices are retained in src-tauri/licenses
and included in desktop bundles.

Brr's MCP Apps host uses the official @modelcontextprotocol/ext-apps SDK (MIT)
and Model Context Protocol client/core libraries (Apache-2.0).
Their licenses and transitive dependency notices are retained in
src-tauri/licenses/mcp-apps-THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt and included in desktop bundles.

Brr's desktop interface uses the Archivo variable font, Copyright 2020 The
Archivo Project Authors, under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. The font and its
full license are retained in public/assets/fonts and included in the app assets.

Brr workspace terminals use xterm.js and its Fit addon (MIT), and portable-pty
(MIT). Their upstream licenses are retained in src-tauri/licenses and included
in desktop bundles.

Brr’s semantic chat editor uses Lexical and @lexical packages (MIT), Copyright
Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates. Their upstream license is retained at
src-tauri/licenses/lexical-LICENSE.txt and included in desktop bundles.
